        ],
        "text": "For publication fiscal year 2024, the validated query result shows 1234 tender invitation notices published (the metric counts published tender invitation notices, used here as the measure of bid invitations)."
      },
      {
        "evidence_ids": [
          "ev_bb1af4fa9dd745dbbad1",
          "ev_abfd7bd477c244b6a266"
        ],
        "text": "The Project Appraisal Document identifies procurement process delays at ERA as a risk rated Substantial, caused by the lack of standard bidding documents for Design and Build works, which leads to protracted preparation and approval and many clarification requests by bidders."
      },
      {
        "evidence_ids": [
          "ev_bb1af4fa9dd745dbbad1",
          "ev_abfd7bd477c244b6a266"
        ],
        "text": "The proposed mitigation is to customise bid documents based on pre-approved Output Performance Road Contract (OPRC) documents, with bidding documents prepared and agreed prior to Negotiations."
      },
      {
        "evidence_ids": [
          "ev_abfd7bd477c244b6a266"
        ],
        "text": "A further delay risk, rated Moderate, is protracted bid evaluation due to the two-envelope system and disparities between bids under the design and build approach, with report quality below standard; mitigation includes training of the evaluation team and TA support."
      },
      {
        "evidence_ids": [
          "ev_77725b4bed1e450f81f3"
        ],
        "text": "The PAD narrative lists the key ERA risks as procurement delays from non-standard bidding documents and elongated evaluation from the two-envelope system, plus delays in approval processes from a long iterative process; it notes ERA will strengthen its internal quality assurance system to submit quality procurement documents."
      }
    ],
